Template: homelab-domain-admin/db_host
Type: string
Default: localhost
Description: PostgreSQL host to bootstrap this app's roles/schema on:
 Used only once, at first install, to run homelab-bootstrap-app-role.

Template: homelab-domain-admin/pgbouncer_host
Type: string
Default: localhost
Description: PgBouncer host to register this app's runtime role with:
 Used only once, at first install. Also written into config.yml's
 database.host, so the running service connects through the pooler.

Template: homelab-domain-admin/api_base
Type: string
Default: http://localhost:3000
Description: Base URL where homelab-api is reachable:
 Written into config.yml's homelab_api.base_url — every request this
 app handles is authenticated by introspecting the caller's JWT here.

Template: homelab-domain-admin/listen_port
Type: string
Default: 2511
Description: Port for homelab-domain-admin to listen on:

Template: homelab-domain-admin/pdns_api_host
Type: string
Default: 127.0.0.1
Description: Host where PowerDNS's own HTTP API is (or will be) reachable:
 Written into config.yml's powerdns.api_base_url. This package enables
 that API itself (see README.md) if PowerDNS is installed locally —
 only change this from 127.0.0.1 if PowerDNS runs on a different host.

Template: homelab-domain-admin/pdns_api_port
Type: string
Default: 8081
Description: Port for PowerDNS's own HTTP API:

Template: homelab-domain-admin/pdns_api_key
Type: password
Description: PowerDNS API key (blank = auto-generate):
 Leave blank when PowerDNS is installed locally on this same host (the
 default deployment topology -- see README.md) -- this package
 generates a random key itself and writes it into PowerDNS's own config
 alongside its own. Required when pdns_api_host points at a REMOTE
 PowerDNS instead: that host's API key already exists and this package
 has no way to reach in and set it, so it must be supplied here to
 match exactly what that PowerDNS is already configured with.

Template: homelab-domain-admin/advertise_host
Type: string
Default: 127.0.0.1
Description: This host's own address to advertise in the service registry:
 Written into config.yml's registry.host -- what homelab-api's gateway
 actually connects to when forwarding /api/v1/domains/* requests here.
 Leave as 127.0.0.1 only if this service runs on the SAME host as
 homelab-api itself; set it to this host's real reachable address
 (e.g. its data-plane IP) for any distributed deployment, or every
 gateway forward will try to reach homelab-api's own loopback instead
 of this service.

Template: homelab-domain-admin/haproxy_vip
Type: string
Default: 10.50.2.44
Description: HAProxy VIP that fronts the domain-admin/signer pool:
 Written into config.yml's registry.host -- what homelab-api's gateway
 connects to when forwarding /api/v1/domains/* requests. This is the
 "always behind HAProxy" convention: even a single signer registers the
 VIP (not its own address), so scaling to 2/3 signers is purely additive
 (one more HAProxy backend server) with no client/gateway change. The
 real per-host backend address (what HAProxy forwards TO) comes from
 advertise_host, which is registered as a backend server on the HAProxy
 host at install.

Template: homelab-domain-admin/key_encryption_key
Type: password
Description: DKIM key-encryption-key (KEK), base64 (blank = auto-generate):
 A 32-byte AES-256-GCM key that wraps each DKIM private key before it is
 stored in the shared homelab DB, so the DB can distribute keys across the
 signer pool without a dump/backup leaking them (see
 Homelab::DomainAdmin::KeyVault). It must be the SAME value on EVERY signer
 host. Leave blank on the FIRST signer and this package generates one and
 prints it -- copy that exact value into this answer on the other signers.
 Keep it OUT of the database and back it up separately; losing it means
 every DKIM key must be regenerated.

Template: homelab-domain-admin/runtime_role
Type: string
Description: Existing runtime DB role (blank = bootstrap a fresh one):
 For an ADDITIONAL signer whose Postgres role already exists in the shared
 homelab DB (this host can't bootstrap it -- no DB admin access): preseed
 the pool's existing runtime role + password + migrate role/password here,
 and the postinst reuses them instead of bootstrapping. Leave all four
 blank on the FIRST signer, where homelab-bootstrap-app-role creates them.

Template: homelab-domain-admin/runtime_password
Type: password
Description: Existing runtime DB role password (for an additional signer):

Template: homelab-domain-admin/migrate_role
Type: string
Description: Existing migrate DB role (for an additional signer):

Template: homelab-domain-admin/migrate_password
Type: password
Description: Existing migrate DB role password (for an additional signer):
